## Price Comparison: Round Brilliant vs Radiant Cut

Radiant cuts are consistently 20–28% cheaper than round brilliants at equivalent stated grades. This discount exists for three reasons:
1. Radiant cuts retain more rough diamond material during cutting — less waste
2. Demand for round brilliants is dramatically higher than for radiant cuts
3. The absence of a GIA cut grade makes radiant harder to price-compare, reducing competition and demand

Ring totals below use the [Knife Edge Solitaire in 14k White Gold at $925](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/knife-edge-solitaire-by-james-allen-item-316048?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational).

