> "The price gap between round brilliant and radiant is not noise — it is structural. Radiant costs less because GIA doesn't grade it, demand is lower, and rough diamond recovery is higher. None of these things affect the actual appearance of a well-cut radiant on the finger. A radiant cut to table 61–68%, depth 61–67%, Very Good polish and symmetry, viewed in HD video — that is a beautiful diamond. You just have to verify it yourself instead of trusting a GIA Excellent stamp." — Farzana Hasan, **[Diamond Critics](https://diamondcritics.com/about-farzana/)**

